    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9828" root="خب" body-key="x">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خُبٌّ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خَبٌّ</span>. ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خِبَّةٌ</span>. Hence <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ثَوْبٌ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَخْبَابٌ</span>: see, again, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خِبَّةٌ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَخْبَابُ الفَحِثِ</span> <i>The</i>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَوَايَا</span> [or <i>winding guts,</i> or <i>intestines into which
the food passes from the stomach</i>]: (K:) thus
used in the pl. form, as though pl. of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خُبٌّ</span>. (TA.) ＝ 
 
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A3-  Also The <i>bark</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لِحَآء</span>) <i>of a tree.</i> (JK, K.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A4- 
And <i>Low,</i> or <i>depressed,</i> land: (JK, K:) pl. [of
pauc.] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَخْبَابٌ</span> and [of mult.] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خُبُوبٌ</span>. (TA.)

